 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? Not rude at all, it' easy for the waiter, and shows you' genuinely like to pay rather than put it off. You can split it evenly and round down if someone was barely served, or go by who had what drinks if that makes more sense. Ten dollars per person is usually seen fair, with a few dollars if the place was particularly good. Some places have minimum though, so watch for a sign the waiter keeps track of. You' welcome. The waitstaff appreciate knowing exactly how much rather than asking each one and having different answers.",
